Il llama.cpp vendorizzato non ha una cartella .git, quindi a ogni configurazione CMake
common/CMakeLists.txt stampa un warning "Git repository not found" per ogni ABI. Il build info
resta ai valori predefiniti e l'app non lo usa: il messaggio passa da WARNING a STATUS.
Riapplicata in automatico da feature/ai/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt.

diff --git a/third-party/llama-cpp/common/CMakeLists.txt b/third-party/llama-cpp/common/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/third-party/llama-cpp/common/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/third-party/llama-cpp/common/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ if(EXISTS "${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/.git")
         message(WARNING "Git index not found in git repository.")
     endif()
 else()
-    message(WARNING "Git repository not found; to enable automatic generation of build info, make sure Git is installed and the project is a Git repository.")
+    message(STATUS "Git repository not found; to enable automatic generation of build info, make sure Git is installed and the project is a Git repository.")
 endif()

 set(TEMPLATE_FILE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/build-info.cpp.in")
